+/*
+ * Modified for the active spherical wheel project (gazebo/physics/README.md).
+ * Upstream: gz-sim 8.10.0, src/systems/physics/Physics.cc (Apache-2.0).
+ * Changes, all marked "ASW exact state":
+ *   1. Every link's world pose and velocities are written to the ECM on every
+ *      step, instead of only links whose pose moved by more than 1e-6.
+ *   2. Pose and vector change detection compares components exactly, so a
+ *      value is never left stale because it moved by less than 1e-6.
+ *   3. DART's automatic deactivation ("sleeping", on by default in DART 6.19)
+ *      is switched off: it freezes a skeleton that stays slow for 0.5 s,
+ *      skipping gravity and contacts, which a balancing robot must never do.
+ * Physics, contact and joint handling are otherwise identical to upstream.
+ */
 /*
